This appears to be a CBP ruling covering three isolators (aseptic and containment). The likely classification is 8421.39 (filtering or purifying machinery for gases) or 9027 or 8419.

Considering the options: isolators with HEPA filtration, VHP decontamination and PLC control are glove-box-type enclosures. CBP has classified similar pharmaceutical isolators under 8421.39.8090 (other filtering or purifying machinery for gases) as machines whose essential function is air filtration to maintain a controlled environment. The alternative, 8419.20 (medical, surgical or laboratory sterilizers), is a weaker fit because the primary function is not sterilization. The VHP cycle decontaminates the chamber itself, but the isolator's main purpose is to provide a sterile working environment through filtration and pressure control. I am going with 8421.39.8090 for all three items.

{"hts_code": "8421.39.8090", "reason": "The isolators are machinery whose essential function is HEPA filtration and pressure-controlled air purification to maintain a controlled environment, so they fall under other filtering or purifying machinery for gases in heading 8421."}
